    orcid: ""

abstract: >
  EISForge is an open-source Python framework for automated electrochemical
  analysis of the Alcohol Oxidation Reaction (AOR). It combines classical
  CNLS fitting (with robust Huber IRLS re-weighting) and Kramers-Kronig
  validation, CV/LSV/EIS analysis, ECSA calculation, Koutecky-Levich
  analysis, scan-rate kinetics (b-value, Randles-Sevcik linearity),
  chronoamperometry stability metrics, AICc multi-model circuit ranking,
  rule-based EIS interpretation, a literature-guided knowledge base
  (parameter priors for 28 electrochemical systems, distilled from a
  survey of over 200 papers), and a Physics-Informed Transformer architecture
  (EIS-GPT). Supports Gamry (.dta), BioLogic (.mpt/.mpr), Ivium (.idf),
  and generic CSV file formats. Includes a live Streamlit web demo.

